    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d272">

                <pb facs="0451" n="357" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg357"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-07-14"><hi rendition="#italic">July 14,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 28.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence
                    relative to the restrictions upon the importation of Canadian cattle into this
                    Kingdom, I have the honor to inclose herewith for the information of yourself
                    and of the Secretary of Agriculture a report which has appeared in to-day’s
                    Times of the reception yesterday by the president of the British board of
                    agriculture of a deputation headed by the Earl of Aberdeen, the newly appointed
                    Governor-General of Canada, which waited upon him for the purpose of urging the
                    removal of the restrictions in question.</p>
                <p>It will be observed that Mr. Gardner regretted his inability to comply with the
                    suggestion of the deputation.</p>
                <p>Therefore, while these restrictions are so rigidly retained upon Canadian cattle,
                    it goes without saying that no relaxation can be expected upon those upon
                    importation of cattle from the United States.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
